## MAJ

### CORR-001 + SAFE-001 (same defect from 2 lenses): target_repo extraction uses re.search first-match

**Bug:** scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh target_repo extraction (around lines 183-194) uses re.search (first-match) with only a not-match guard. cascade_status was fixed in fix-round-1 (replaced re.search with re.findall + len==1 assertion); target_repo was missed.

**Bypass:** a DISPATCH-NOTE with two `**Target:** ...` lines silently accepts the first match. Decoy-first layout (stale or wrong target line first; correct target second) passes the log-entry target match against the wrong adopter — log entry exists for adopter X, but the script reports the diff matched the decoy adopter Y.

**Fix:** in scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:
1. Replace re.search for target_repo with re.findall.
2. Add `len(matches) == 1` assertion. If 0 matches OR ≥2, exit 1 with diagnostic naming the count + the matched values (mirror the cascade_status pattern from fix-round-1).
3. Update the diagnostic message: `ERROR: expected exactly one **Target:** match in DISPATCH-NOTE, found N: [list]`

In tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:
1. Add a test case where DISPATCH-NOTE has TWO `**Target:**` lines (e.g. first `jrnb2024/wrong`, second `jrnb2024/pim`) → run_case asserting exit 1 + diagnostic naming the 2 matches.
2. Verify the existing target-match positive cases still pass.

Update D-044 row in docs/DECISIONS.md to reflect the additional exactly-one assertion on target_repo (alongside cascade_status).

